# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the unit tests.
#
# Only for leaks that are *faithful to the original binary* and therefore
# deliberately not fixed. Anything else should be fixed, not suppressed - the
# whole value of running the suites under the sanitizer preset is that it fails.
#
# Usage:
#   LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/lsan.supp \
#     ./out/build/linux-x64-asan/tests/arcanum-tests
#
# mes_load_internal: a .mes file that opens but parses to zero entries leaks the
# data buffer allocated for it - `mes_load` returns false without freeing it.
# The original does the same: 0x4D4317..0x4D4333 sets the handle to -1 and
# returns 0 with no free call. See the NOTE in src/game/mes.c.
leak:mes_load_internal
